<https://uor.foundation/division/> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "UOR Division Algebras"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The four normed division algebras R, C, H, O and the Cayley-Dickson construction."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/> <https://uor.foundation/space> "kernel"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://uor.foundation/op/> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://uor.foundation/convergence/> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/NormedDivisionAlgebra> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/NormedDivisionAlgebra> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "NormedDivisionAlgebra"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/NormedDivisionAlgebra> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An algebra over R that is a division ring with multiplicative norm. Exactly four exist (Hurwitz theorem): R, C, H, O."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/NormedDivisionAlgebra> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/CayleyDicksonConstruction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/CayleyDicksonConstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CayleyDicksonConstruction"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/CayleyDicksonConstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The doubling construction that builds each division algebra from the previous: R → C → H → O."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/CayleyDicksonConstruction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/MultiplicationTable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/MultiplicationTable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MultiplicationTable"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/MultiplicationTable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The explicit product rules for a division algebra’s basis elements."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/MultiplicationTable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/AlgebraCommutator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/AlgebraCommutator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "AlgebraCommutator"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/AlgebraCommutator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The commutator [a,b] = ab − ba. Zero for R and C; non-zero for H and O."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/AlgebraCommutator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/AlgebraAssociator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/AlgebraAssociator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "AlgebraAssociator"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/AlgebraAssociator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The associator [a,b,c] = (ab)c − a(bc). Zero for R, C, H; non-zero for O."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://uor.foundation/division/AlgebraAssociator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
